.nh
.TH "SYMVAULT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Symaira Vault" "Symaira Vault Manual"

.SH NAME
symvault-device-approval-revoke - Revoke an approval device's ability to approve/deny requests


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsymvault device approval-revoke  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Revoke a device enrolled via 'symvault device approval-pair', so it can
no longer approve or deny agent credential requests. This does NOT
re-encrypt or otherwise affect vault entries — it only invalidates that
device's approval-decision bearer token. For revoking a vault-content sync
device instead, use 'symvault device revoke \&' (a different, more
destructive command that re-encrypts every entry).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for approval-revoke

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip confirmation prompt


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	When to emit ANSI color: auto, always, never

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output format shorthand for --output json; overrides --output when both are specified

.PP
\fB--no-pipe-warning\fP[=false]
	suppress 'reading from non-TTY' warning when piping secrets

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	Output format (text, json, yaml)

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	use a named vault profile

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB--theme\fP=""
	Color preset: default, highcontrast, colorblind (or SYMVAULT_THEME)

.PP
\fB--vault\fP="~/.symvault"
	path to the password vault


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  symvault device approval-list
  symvault device approval-revoke dev-abc123
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsymvault-device(1)\fP
